  "title": "EVM launch + bundle forensics"
 },
 "description": "Who bundled an EVM token launch (Base, BSC, Ethereum, Arbitrum, Robinhood and 13 more): creation-tx airdrops to fake holders, first-seconds buys, scripted fixed-cadence buying, fresh-wallet and transfer-only holders, dev holdings, exchange-labelled holders, GoPlus contract flags \u2014 plus a skip/pass verdict. Replays every ERC-20 Transfer of the token from its first mint on the public RPC, so for young tokens (Base ~4 days, BSC ~6 h of history in budget) holder balances, buys and wallet-to-wallet hand-offs are exact. Launchpads (Four.meme, Uniswap v4 PoolManager, v2/v3 pairs from Dexscreener) are detected; vault/locker contracts that never bought are kept out of the wallet rules, while contracts that DID buy (smart wallets, bundler contracts) count as wallets. Older tokens fall back to GoPlus holders with 527 exchange wallets named. Skip rules: GoPlus honeypot/tax>10%/owner powers; top-10 wallets >35%; first ~2 s of buys >20%; >10% held by wallets that never bought; creation tx airdropping \u226510 wallets or >10%; scripted buying (\u22655 buys \u22651% at a regular cadence taking \u226515%); fresh wallets / buyer contracts >15%. Heuristic on EVM (mirrors the back-tested Solana guard); \"pass\" is not a safety promise. When to use: Bundles and who holds an EVM token launch (Base/BSC first-class); for contract-only flags use evm_token_security (on the MAD Synapse \u00b7 Wallets & Risk server, https://agent.maddegen.art/hub/mcp/risk). Price: $0.005 per call (10 free/day; after that a payment-required result lists x402 options). Errors: returns isError with a message for invalid input or an upstream failure (not charged).",
